            h1 Closure
            a(href="https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/still-confused-by-move-vs-closures/1430") understanding rust closure
            pre
                code.
                    let x = || {println!("Hello")};  

            p this statement creates instance of struct having data and method  

            //Ashu and call are my given names rust will create names in its own way 

            pre
                code.
                    struct Ashu{ 
                        //variables
                    }
                    impl Ashu{
                        //call can take &self or &mut self
                        fn call(&self){
                            println!("Hello")
                        }
                    }

            p now this struct will be initialized in memory and the method can access struct mutably or immutably

            h2 capturing environment  
            p normally functions can access values created inside it or passed as argument but closures can access the value in the same scope  

            pre
                code.
                    fn main(){
                        let y = 1;
                        //y will be accessed in the closure even after it is not available in the x declaration of closure  
                        //y can be passed as &y or &mut y (if y is mutable itself)
                        //giving ownership to closure
                        //move will pass ownership of y to closure and closure can consume y
                        let x = || {println!("{}",y)}; 
                    }


